Requires `poster_badges` and up to 4 sets declared in `ether.contributes.posterBadges: [{key, label, description?}]` (`key` matching `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$`), such as a `"dub languages"` set (`key: "dub_languages"`, `label: "Dub languages"`) for an anime plugin or an `"editions"` set (`key: "editions"`, `label: "Editions"`).

```ts
ether.badges.set("dub_languages", [
  { title: { type: "show", tmdb: 37854 }, labels: ["EN DUB", "JA"] },
]);
ether.badges.set("editions", [
  { title: { type: "movie", imdb: "tt0083658" }, labels: ["FINAL CUT"] },
]);
const usage = ether.badges.usage(); // { titles, quotaTitles }
// ether.badges.clear("editions");
```

`set(setKey, entries)` accepts up to 500 entries per call; empty `labels` deletes that title's badges in the set. At most 3 labels per title per set are allowed, each 1 to 16 characters from `[A-Z0-9 +&'./-]` (lowercase input is uppercased, anything else is rejected), up to 200,000 badged titles per plugin. Ether draws the badges itself, the owner can switch each set off in Metadata -> Artwork (`disabledBadgeSets`), and no plugin call happens while rendering.

