upsert/delete/items require catalog_provider and your own declared kind. upsert/delete only work for push-mode kinds; pull sync owns its writes. Push writes are journalled for undo (kept up to 30 days, 10,000 entries, or 256 MiB per plugin); unchanged items with matching content hashes are never snapshotted, and kinds may set sync.undo: "ids" to record only created and touched IDs (skipping snapshot reads, with undo deleting only created items). items is cursor-paged and unfiltered. Items are validated against declared levels and fields. Unknown custom fields are dropped; invalid types reject the item.

For frontend adapters serving their own protocol, visible and browse apply the library's Rules, library grants, and viewer content safety for the requesting viewer (same LibraryPolicy as the console and built-in projectors). Both require frontend_adapter and an authenticated frontend adapter request; non-adapter calls fail with permission denied. Viewer identity comes only from Ether's authenticated request context (and request-scoped X-Ether-Viewer-Token on remote callbacks), never guest input. visible accepts at most 500 IDs per call.

```ts
const page = ether.kinds.items("recordings", "", 50);
// Inside a frontend adapter request:
const allowed = ether.kinds.visible("recordings", ["rec-1", "rec-2"]);
const filtered = ether.kinds.browse("recordings", { query: "live", limit: 50 });
```

