Cache refs are content addressed blob:<sha256>, never filesystem paths. A library defaults to 2 GiB under a shared min(10 GiB, 5% of cache disk) cap; manifest and owner settings can override it. Remote blob uploads cap at 256 MiB. Call `cache.delete(blobRef)` to remove a temporary blob from your own cache namespaces and free its quota immediately so large temporaries do not evict smaller kept files; deleting an absent or already evicted ref succeeds. Use kinds for metadata and cache for bytes.

```ts
const ref = ether.cache.put("library-key", "cover.txt", "hello");
const data = ether.cache.open(ref);
ether.cache.delete(ref);
```

