Mint a scoped, short-lived URL for one of your own kind items with frontend.streamURL (accepting an optional positional partIndex or { partIndex?, source?, absolute?, wait? } to pin a zero-based part, pin an exact resolver PlayableSource.id with no failover, or return an absolute URL using the request's X-Ether-Origin with fallback to the adapter's first published address), and evaluate the library's Rules and viewer access policy with kinds.visible (up to 500 IDs) or kinds.browse. Authenticated adapter requests also receive X-Ether-Origin (scheme://host[:port][/prefix], honouring trusted proxies only with inbound client values stripped) alongside X-Ether-Viewer. The authenticated viewer comes from the frontend adapter request context (and X-Ether-Viewer-Token on remote callbacks), never guest-supplied input. Embed the stream URL in the protocol response; Ether serves the bytes without proxying through your plugin. Raw hosted spelling is streamURL; the TypeScript SDK uses streamUrl.

```ts
const page = ether.kinds.browse("comic", { limit: 50 });
const allowed = ether.kinds.visible("comic", ["c1", "c2"]);
const url = ether.frontend.streamURL("item-ref");
const exact = ether.frontend.streamURL("item-ref", { source: "epub" });
const abs = ether.frontend.streamURL("item-ref", { absolute: true });
```

