Uses the owner's configured language model from Settings -> Integrations -> Language model (one AI, one connection place; never ask for a second API key). Requires `permissions.ai: "complete"` (or `"complete+search"` to also opt in to bounded, cached interactive search calls), shown on the install sheet and revocable live in plugin permissions (`ai` and `ai.search`). No model credentials, endpoint URLs, or raw provider errors ever reach the plugin.

```ts
try {
  const res = ether.ai.complete({
    messages: [
      { role: "system", content: "Extract structured search filters." },
      { role: "user", content: "90s sci-fi films without horror" },
    ],
    schema: {
      type: "object",
      required: ["genres"],
      properties: {
        decade: { type: "integer" },
        genres: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
        excludeGenres: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
      },
      additionalProperties: false,
    },
    maxTokens: 256,
  });
  // res.json is already parsed and validated against schema; res.text holds canonical JSON.
} catch (err) {
  if ((err as { code?: string }).code === "not_configured") {
    // Owner has not configured a language model: fall back cleanly.
  }
}
```

## Route policy & search opt-in
With `permissions.ai: "complete"`, `ai.complete` is allowed only on owner actions (`/ether/action/*`), background jobs (`/ether/job/*`), Flow actions (`/ether/v1/flow-actions/*`), tools (`/ether/tool/*`), event handlers (`/ether/event`), setup/test routes (`/ether/v1/setup/*`, `/ether/test`), background kind/Live TV sync, or declared `ether.schedule` routes. Precompute or cache structured results in `ether.kv` for browse/playback paths.

To use `ai.complete` during interactive search (matching Ether's own descriptive search exception), declare `permissions.ai: "complete+search"`. This adds a separate install-sheet line ("Uses your language model while a viewer searches") and an independently revocable `ai.search` grant, and opens ONLY:
- Stremio-style catalog search routes with a non-empty `search` query (`/catalog/{type}/{id}/search=….json`; non-search catalog browse and empty `search=` stay refused),
- Media-kind search routes (`/ether/v1/kinds/{kind}/search` with a non-empty query; `/resolve`, `/match`, `/items`, and `/live` stay refused),
- Declared frontend adapter search routes (`/ether/v1/frontend/{key}/…` matching `contributes.frontendAdapters[].searchPaths`, or conventional `/search`, `/search2`, `/search3` subpaths when `searchPaths` is omitted) with a non-empty query (`searchQuery` in the request body is required for routes without a URL query parameter such as GraphQL POST endpoints).

Every other viewer/client path (`/stream/*`, non-search `/catalog/*`, `/meta/*`, `/subtitles/*`, `/ether/open*`, `/ether/metadata/*`, `/ether/subtitles/*`, `/ether/markers*`, `/ether/v1/kinds/*/resolve|match|items|live`, non-search `/ether/v1/frontend/*`, `/ether/view/*`, `/ether/options/*`, `/ether/health`, `/ether/configure`, `/ether/file/*`, `/ether/directory/*`, and hot-path `rank_key`/`cond_match`) stays refused. Remote plugins forward `X-Ether-Viewer-Token` on frontend-adapter search calls (handled automatically by the SDKs) so the host enforces the active adapter route, viewer rate limit, and live grant.

## Bounds, caching & error codes
Safe per-plugin defaults apply with no extra owner settings: 1..20 messages (`system`, `user`, `assistant`, with at least one `user`), 32 KiB total prompt bytes, 32 KiB JSON Schema (external `$ref` URLs are rejected), `maxTokens` default 1024 / max 4096, `temperature` in `[0, 2]`, and 64 KiB response cap.
- Background/action routes: 20 calls/minute per plugin, `timeoutMs` default/max 30 s.
- Interactive search routes (`complete+search`): hard per-request ceiling `timeoutMs` <= 20 s (matching Ether's own descriptive search bound; always catch `timeout`/`deadline` and return non-AI results), per-query host caching (10 min TTL, 256 entries per plugin, normalized query + request fingerprint, concurrent in-flight dedup) so repeated searches do not re-ask the model, and a separate per-viewer rate limit (10 uncached calls/minute per viewer) that never spends the background budget.

Error codes (`err.code` in JS/TS/Python, `HostError.Code` in Go): `not_configured` (HTTP 501 — no language model configured; does not consume rate limit), `forbidden` (hosted) / `permission_denied` (HTTP 403 remote — missing/revoked `ai` or `ai.search` grant, missing `searchQuery`, or disallowed client route), `rate_limited` (HTTP 429), `invalid_input` (hosted) / `invalid` (HTTP 400 remote), `invalid_output` (HTTP 502 — reply was not valid JSON, oversized, or failed `schema`), `timeout` (hosted) / `deadline` (HTTP 504 remote — return non-AI search results), `unavailable` (HTTP 503 — provider call failed, sanitized).

