Reads container metadata (`{durationSec, container, width, height, sizeBytes}`) for any `PlayableSource` in the same shape `/resolve` returns, reusing Ether's durable `release_probes` cache. Requires `permissions.media: "probe"` (shown on the install sheet as "Probes media container metadata" and revocable live as `media`).

```ts
const probe = ether.media.probe({
  id: "ep-01",
  pattern: "release",
  mime: "video/x-matroska",
  release: { infoHash, fileIndex: 1 },
});
// probe => { durationSec: 2280.4, container: "mkv", width: 1920, height: 1080, sizeBytes: 1234567890 }
```

## Route policy & bounds
`media.probe` is allowed only on jobs (`/ether/job/*`), actions (`/ether/action/*`), Flow actions, tools, event handlers, setup/test routes, feed routes, background kind/Live TV sync, or declared `ether.schedule` routes. Every interactive viewer or client request path (`/resolve`, `/search`, `/catalog/*`, `/stream/*`, `/meta/*`, `/subtitles/*`, `/ether/v1/frontend/*`, `/ether/view/*`, `/ether/options/*`, `/ether/health`, `/ether/configure`, and remote calls carrying `X-Ether-Viewer-Token`) is refused. Each call is bounded at 10 s and per-plugin rate-limited (60 calls/minute). Release probes run strictly cached-only without queuing uncached debrid downloads; URL, folder, secret, and blob permissions still apply per source pattern.

For playback-time verification without calling `media.probe`, set both `durationSec` and `durationToleranceSec` (> 0) on a `PlayableSource` returned by `/resolve`: Ether probes the container header on open (reusing `release_probes`) and rejects mismatches beyond `durationToleranceSec` as wrong content so the next candidate is tried.

